:: Gwylan Strong Wings Ask
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>><<speechresolve>>
<<npc Gwylan>><<person1>>
<<if !Transformations.hasDivineWings()>>
	You start to ask about your wings.
	<br><br>
	Gwylan looks past your shoulder at your back, then back at your face.
	"You'll need to bring the wings with you, dear. I can't put strength into something that isn't there."
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<elseif Transformations.hasGwylanStrengthenedWings()>>
	<<set _wingStrengthDays to Math.max(1, Time.date.dayDifference(new DateTime(V.gwylan.wingStrength)))>>
	Gwylan takes the front edge of one wing between two fingers and presses.
	<br><br>
	"My work is still in there. Use it while you have it." <<He>> lets go.
	"<span class="blue">Another <<number _wingStrengthDays>> <<pluralise _wingStrengthDays "day">>, near enough.
	Come back when they go soft again.</span>"
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<elseif Transformations.hasNaturalFlightWings()>>
	Gwylan runs a hand along the front edge of one wing, stopping where the muscle is thickest.
	"These carry you already. Anything I added would only get in the way."
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<elseif $gwylan.request.special is "strong wings">>
	"I haven't forgotten," Gwylan says, tapping the list on the counter. "Bring me everything on there,
	and I'll start the preparation."
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<elseif $gwylan.wingPotionReady>>
	Gwylan points at the cabinet behind <<him>> without looking up. "One at a time, dear. Yours is in there already."
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<elseif $gwylan.request.event>>
	You spread your wings behind you. "Can you make these strong enough to fly?"
	<br><br>
	Gwylan glances at the shelves, then at you. "Possibly. You've already promised me something else,
	though, and I'd rather not have two jobs going at once. Finish that first."
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<elseif $gwylanSeen.includes("strong_wings_treatment")>>
	You turn your back to <<him>> and spread your wings without being asked.
	<br><br>
	Gwylan puts down what <<hes>> holding and runs a thumb along the root of one wing, the same as last time.
	"Soft again," <<he>> says. "I did wonder how long you'd last. Let me see what I have in stock."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Ask what <<he>> needs this time|Gwylan Strong Wings Examine 3]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek" "shy">>You ease your wings open behind you. "C-Could you make them stronger? Strong enough to fly with?"
		<<case "polite" "docile">>You spread your wings carefully, keeping them clear of the shelves. "Could you make my wings strong enough to fly with?"
		<<case "flamboyant">>You throw your wings open and hold the pose. "They're beautiful. Beautiful things should be in the air. Can you make them strong enough?"
		<<case "bratty" "cruel">>You flare your wings. "These should be able to carry me, and they don't. Fix that."
		<<case "confident" "special">>You spread your wings. "I want to fly with these. Can you make them strong enough?"
		<<default>>You spread your wings. "Can you make them strong enough to fly with?"
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	Gwylan doesn't answer. <<He>> caps the jar <<hes>> been labelling, comes out from behind the counter,
	and walks a slow circle around you. Behind you <<he>> stops, lifts your hair off your neck,
	and looks at the place where the wings join your back.
	<br><br>
	Then <<he>> crosses to the front door, slides the bolt across, and draws the curtain over the window by the counter.
	The shop goes dim.
	<br><br>
	<<if $hypnosis_traits.devotion gte 3>>
		<<hypnosisText "You hear the bolt go across and stop worrying. <<He>> has decided what happens next, so you don't have to.">>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	"Stand still for me," <<he>> says, coming back. "I won't promise you anything until I've had my hands on them."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Let <<him>> examine your wings|Gwylan Strong Wings Examine]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Examine
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
Gwylan puts one hand flat between your shoulder blades and pushes. Your chest comes forward,
and the wings lift away from your back. <<His>> other hand finds the joint at the root and presses a thumb into the muscle.
"Push against me."
<br><br>
You push. <<He>> moves <<his>> thumb a finger's width along and has you do it again, then again,
working outwards until <<he>> reaches the first bend.
<br><br>
"Open them as far as the shelves let you."
<br><br>
You spread the wing. Gwylan follows it outwards, holding the weight on <<his>> forearm and opening each joint in turn,
until the tip rests in <<his>> palm.
<<He>> holds a feather up to the lamp and turns it slowly, then draws <<his>> hand back down the whole length of the wing.
Your shoulders shiver. <<arousal 100>><<garousal>>
<br><br>
"Once more. Beat them, hard as you like."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Gwylan Strong Wings Examine 2]]>><<pass 2>><</link>>
<br>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Examine 2
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
You bring them down. Paper lifts off the counter, and a bundle of dried flowers swings on its hook.
Gwylan catches the bundle before it comes off the nail, laughing.
<br><br>
"They're built properly," <<he>> says. "Everything is where it should be. There just isn't enough of it."
<br><br>
<<He>> holds <<his>> own wrist up beside the root of your wing. "A hawk your size carries a bone through here
thicker than this, and half its chest is the muscle that pulls that bone down.
Yours grew from a picture of wings. Whatever changed you copied the shape and left out the muscle that works it."
<br><br>
You start to ask, and <<he>> answers before you finish. "Yes. I can put weight into them. Not for good...
your body knows what it's meant to look like, and it pulls them back to that within the week.
Seven days in the air, then you're gliding again."
<br><br>
<<He>> holds up one finger before you can be pleased about it. "Strength gets you off the ground.
It won't keep you up there. Air moves in layers, and it changes without warning.
It can hold your left wing up while your right one drops. Nothing I brew will teach your body to feel that coming.
You have to learn it from an animal that was born doing it."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Gwylan Strong Wings Examine 3]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Examine 3
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
<<if $birdFly isnot 1>>
	<<He>> looks towards the window facing the moor, and takes a while to say the next part.
	"There's something living out that way. Everyone believes its kind died out years ago.
	If it takes to you, it can teach you the half I can't."
	<br><br>
	<<if $syndromebird is 1>>
		You know at once who <<hes>> talking about. "You mean my spouse."
		<br><br>
		Gwylan's hand stills against your wing. "Do I? I don't know what it calls itself, dear.
		Only that something rare lives out there, and that people with guns would like to know where."
		<<He>> folds your wing closed against your back and pats it. "But if you've already found each other,
		you don't need directions from me. Ask your spouse to teach you."
	<<else>>
		"What is it?" you ask.
		<br><br>
		Gwylan folds your wing closed against your back and pats it. "If I put a name to it,
		you'll say that name to somebody, and somebody will say it to a man with a gun. That's how the last of them went."
		<<He>> straightens your hair where <<he>> moved it. "Go out onto the moor. Go somewhere high,
		and be patient, and have some manners. You'll know it when it looks at you."
		<<run $gwylanSeen.pushUnique("strong_wings_hawk")>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<span class="blue">Gwylan cannot give you the instincts needed for flight.
	<<if $syndromebird is 1>>Your spouse may be able to teach you.<<else>>A great bird in the moor may be able to teach you.<</if>></span>
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<else>>
	<<if $gwylanSeen.includes("strong_wings_treatment")>>
		<<He>> pulls the tin box down off the shelf and licks the end of the pencil. "The last lot went into your back,
		so we start from nothing. The list won't be the same either. I use whatever I can get hold of that week."
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		You tell <<him>> about the tower on the moor: the ledge, the drop, and the push that came before you were ready.
		How the ground stopped rushing up at you, and how the Great Hawk circled you until you could keep yourself up on the wind.
		<br><br>
		Gwylan listens with both hands still on your wing. "It pushed you off. Of course it did.
		That's the only way any of them learn."
		<br><br>
		<<if $gwylanSeen.includes("request_preen")>>
			<<He>> is quiet for a moment. "I told you I'd like to see you fly one day. I didn't expect to be asked to arrange it."
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		"Then you've done the dangerous half already, and I'm left with the boring half."
		<<He>> lets your wing fold shut and goes to the shelves, pulling down a tin box and a stub of pencil.
		"Divine flesh throws off nearly everything on these shelves. Whatever I make has to get through on the
		first try, so I'll need good material for it."
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<run gwylanRequest("strongWings")>>
	<<set _wingRare to $gwylan.request.items[0]>>
	<<set _wingMid to $gwylan.request.items[1]>>
	<<set _wingCommon to $gwylan.request.items[2]>>
	<<set _wingRareText to setup.foodstuff[_wingRare.name].plural>>
	<<set _wingMidText to setup.foodstuff[_wingMid.name].plural>>
	<<set _wingCommonText to setup.foodstuff[_wingCommon.name].plural>>
	<<He>> writes three lines and turns the paper around so you can read it.
	<br><br>
	"<span class="gold"><<Number _wingRare.need>> <<= _wingRareText>></span>, first.
	That's the part that does the work, and nothing else will stand in for it, so please don't bring me something similar."
	<<His>> pencil moves down. "<span class="gold"><<Number _wingMid.need>> <<= _wingMidText>></span>
	to hold the effect together once I've drawn it out, or it spoils within the hour.
	And <span class="gold"><<number _wingCommon.need>> <<= _wingCommonText>></span> for bulk,
	so what I rub into you doesn't take the skin off your back."
	<br><br>
	"Once I have all of it, I need <span class="blue">three full days</span>. The first part has to break down slowly.
	If I rush it the whole batch turns bitter, and bitter burns straight through skin."
	<<He>> folds the list and tucks it under the till. "Bring it when you can. Nothing on there spoils quickly."
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold">Gwylan's request has been added to your journal.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<</if>>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Ingredients
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
<<npc Gwylan>><<person1>>
<<if $gwylan.request.special isnot "strong wings">>
	Gwylan looks up, puzzled. "Ingredients for what, dear?"
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<elseif !gwylanRequestMet()>>
	Gwylan looks over what you've brought and shakes <<his>> head.
	"Not all of it. I did tell you, dear. Miss one thing and the rest is no use to me."
	<<He>> slides the list back across the counter to you.
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<<else>>
	<<set _wingRare to $gwylan.request.items[0]>>
	<<set _wingMid to $gwylan.request.items[1]>>
	<<set _wingCommon to $gwylan.request.items[2]>>
	<<set _wingRareText to setup.foodstuff[_wingRare.name].plural>>
	<<set _wingMidText to setup.foodstuff[_wingMid.name].plural>>
	<<set _wingCommonText to setup.foodstuff[_wingCommon.name].plural>>
	You set everything out along the counter in three groups. Gwylan counts each one,
	moving the pieces into line with one finger as <<he>> goes.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> starts with the <<= _wingRareText>>, holding one up to the lamp and turning it.
	<<switch _wingRare.name>>
		<<case "orchid">>
			"People grow these in pots and wonder why they die. Where they come from they hang off bark with their
			roots bare, living on wet air. A plant that lives on air belongs in a mixture made for flying."
		<<case "ghostshroom">>
			"They come up where something ended badly, or so the story goes. What I know for certain is that they
			take hold in flesh that isn't sure what it's supposed to be." <<He>> looks at your back.
			"Which is exactly what I'm working on."
		<<case "strange_flower">>
			"Most of what's made from these ruins people. Prepared carefully, it stops a body from throwing off a
			change it doesn't like. Your wings are going to want to throw this one off."
		<<case "wild_honeycomb">>
			"Wild comb, with the wax still in it. The honey carries the mixture, and the wax keeps it on your skin
			long enough to work. Shop honey has been boiled to death and would just sit there."
		<<case "truffle">>
			"Grown in the dark, feeding through the roots of something much bigger than itself."
			<<He>> smells it, and shuts <<his>> eyes for a second. "That's the trick I want to borrow.
			Feeding the muscle from underneath."
		<<case "wolfshroom">>
			"Stubborn things. They keep wolves off my door and they'll keep your body from arguing,
			which is more or less the same job."
		<<default>>
			"This is the part that does the work. Everything else on the list is here to look after it."
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Gwylan Strong Wings Ingredients 2]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Ingredients 2
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
/* Temp vars don't survive the passage change, so rebuild them from the request. */
<<set _wingItems to $gwylan.request.items or []>>
<<set _wingMid to _wingItems[1]>>
<<set _wingCommon to _wingItems[2]>>
<<if _wingMid>>
<<set _wingMidText to setup.foodstuff[_wingMid.name].plural>>
<<He>> moves on to the <<= _wingMidText>>.
<<switch _wingMid.name>>
	<<case "bird_egg">>
		"Everything a bird needs to become a bird is already inside one of these, sealed up and waiting.
		I want a little of that in the mixture." <<He>> turns one over.
		"I usually have to race every fox in the forest for these. Not this time."
	<<case "mushroom">>
		"Heartshrooms. They drive the blood harder without muddling your head.
		Muscle that's being asked to grow overnight needs the blood."
	<<case "red_rose">>
		"Roses give me the oil to carry the rest into you. They also make the whole business smell
		like something you'd want on your skin, which matters more than you'd think."
	<<case "tulip">>
		"Tulips make me nostalgic, and I've never worked out why." <<He>> smiles at the row of them.
		"They crush down into a very clean base. That's the real reason they're on the list."
	<<case "plumeria">>
		"Oh, these keep their scent through heat. Most flowers give it up the moment I put them near a flame,
		and I'll be reducing this batch for three days."
	<<case "wolfshroom">>
		"Wolfshrooms keep a mixture from separating, long after it should have.
		I go through more of them than anything else in this shop."
	<<default>>
		"These hold the first part together once I've drawn it out. Left on its own it would be gone by supper."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if _wingCommon>>
<<He>> counts the last group twice.
<<switch _wingCommon.name>>
	<<case "salt">>
		"Salt draws the water out so I can reduce it faster, and it takes the sting out of what's left.
		There's very little in here that salt doesn't help."
	<<case "sugar">>
		<<He>> presses a fingertip into the sugar and licks it. "It thickens as it cooks.
		Don't look at me like that, you were going to do the same."
	<<case "vegetable_oil">>
		"Oil is the body of it. The rest needs something plain to sit in, or it burns straight through your skin
		and I end up treating that instead."
	<<case "red_wine" "white_wine">>
		"Wine pulls out what water can't reach, and it cooks away by the third day. You won't be drunk when
		I'm finished with you."
	<<default>>
		"Bulk. Nothing clever about it. It sits between your skin and the part that burns."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Gwylan Strong Wings Ingredients 3]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Ingredients 3
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
Gwylan sweeps all three groups into a wide bowl and carries it to the back room. You hear a drawer,
then a long pour, then nothing for a while. When <<he>> comes back <<his>> sleeves are pushed up to the elbow
and <<his>> hands smell sharp.
<br><br>
"Three days," <<he>> says, writing the date on a paper tag. "It steeps, it settles,
then I strain it and put it somewhere dark. Don't come and ask me on the second day,
because on the second day it's poison."
<br><br>
<<if $hypnosis_traits.devotion gte 2>>
	<<He>> sees your face before you can hide the disappointment, and laughs. "Three days,
	<<pcpetname "Gwylan">>. You've waited longer for worse."
	<br><br>
<</if>>
"One more thing, so it isn't a surprise later. Your body will fight this while I'm working it in,
and a body that fights gets hurt." <<He>> ties the tag onto the bowl. "So you'll be under while I do it.
<span class="purple">You'll need a clear head that day, the same as any of my other work.</span>"
<br><br>
/* This is a service the player asked for, not a favour done for Gwylan, so it must not grant a favour
credit but it must not spend one the player already earned either. */
<<set _favourOwed to $gwylan.requestDone>>
<<run $gwylan.request.items?.forEach(item => {
	if (item.category === "tending" && V.foodstuff[item.name]) V.foodstuff[item.name].amount -= item.need;
})>>
<<gwylanRequestEnd "silent">>
<<set $gwylan.requestDone to _favourOwed>>
<<set $gwylan.wingPotionReady to new DateTime(Time.date).addDays(3).timeStamp>>
<br><br>
<<gwylanOptions>>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Return
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
<<npc Gwylan>><<person1>>
<<if !$gwylan.wingPotionReady>>
	Gwylan tilts <<his>> head. "I don't have anything brewing for your wings, dear."
<<elseif $gwylan.wingPotionReady gt Time.date.timeStamp>>
	<<set _wingPotionDays to Math.max(1, Time.date.dayDifference(new DateTime(V.gwylan.wingPotionReady)))>>
	Gwylan lifts a stoppered bottle from behind the counter, holds it against the lamp, and puts it straight back down.
	"Still cloudy. <span class="blue"><<number _wingPotionDays>> more <<pluralise _wingPotionDays "day">>.</span>
	Ask me again then, and not before."
<<elseif !Transformations.hasDivineWings()>>
	Gwylan reaches for the cabinet, then stops when <<he>> looks past your shoulder. "Your wings have gone.
	This has to be worked into the muscle itself, so there's nothing for me to work it into."
	<<He>> shuts the cabinet again. "It'll keep. Come back when you have them."
<<elseif $plucked>>
	Gwylan turns you by the shoulder and looks at the gaps in your feathers. "Not while you're this bare.
	You'd get a week of strong wings you couldn't use, and I'd have thrown away three days of work.
	Let them grow back first."
<<elseif !$settings.hypnosisEnabled>>
	Gwylan sets a dark bottle on the counter and rests a hand over the stopper. "It's ready.
	It also can't go on you while you're awake, and <span class="blue">you've closed your mind to that sort of thing.</span>
	Open it again, and we'll start."
<<elseif $daily.gwylan.hypnosis>>
	Gwylan sets the bottle down, keeping <<his>> hand over it. "Not today. I've already been inside your head once,
	and doing it twice in a day makes a mess of people." <<He>> puts the bottle away.
	"<span class="blue">Later, when you can be put under again.</span>"
<<else>>
	Gwylan unlocks the low cabinet behind the counter and lifts out a dark glass bottle.
	Pale liquid clings to the sides as <<he>> tilts it. Threads of gold and red move through it, and they slide
	apart every time you try to look straight at them.
	<br><br>
	"There. Strained on the second night, and it's been in the dark since." <<He>> works the stopper loose a fraction,
	sniffs, and pushes it home again. "It has to go into every joint and be worked down into the muscle.
	That takes a while, and it hurts more if you tense up."
	<br><br>
	<<if $gwylanSeen.includes("hypnosis_intro")>>
		"So we do it the way we always do. You go under, I work, and you come back when I've finished."
	<<else>>
		"Which is why you won't be awake for it. I'll put you under, the same as I would for anything else that needs your body to stop fighting me."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<hypnosisicon>><<link [[Go with <<him>> (1:10)|Gwylan Strong Wings Treatment]]>><<pass 20>><</link>><<gwylanHypnoNote>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if !$settings.hypnosisEnabled or $daily.gwylan.hypnosis or $plucked or !$gwylan.wingPotionReady or $gwylan.wingPotionReady gt Time.date.timeStamp or !Transformations.hasDivineWings()>>
	<br><br>
	<<gwylanOptions>>
<</if>>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Treatment
