<<if $phase2 is "no">>
	<<if !$willpowerSuccess>>
		You set the cup down full. Gwylan looks at it, then at you, and picks it back up. "Don't be difficult, dear."
		<br><br>
		<<hypnosisText "Your hands stay in your lap. <span class='red'><<He>> knows what <<hes>> doing.</span>">>
		<br><br>
		<<He>> holds the cup to your mouth and you drink it down while <<he>> strokes the back of your head.
		Your arms are heavy by the time <<he>> takes it away.
		<<stress -12>><<tiredness 3>><<hallucinogen 200>><<set $hypnosis_potency++>><<llstress>><<gtiredness>><<gwylanHypnoEffect>>
	<<else>>
		You put the cup down without touching it. Gwylan raises an eyebrow, moves it aside, and says nothing about it.
	<</if>>
<<elseif $phase2 is "drink">>
	The tea is bitter under the honey. Warmth spreads from your stomach out to your fingers,
	and your shoulders drop.
	<<stress -12>><<tiredness 3>><<hallucinogen 200>><<set $hypnosis_potency++>><<llstress>><<gtiredness>><<gwylanHypnoEffect>>
<<else>>
	You finish what's in the cup and hand it back.
	<<stress -12>><<tiredness 3>><<hallucinogen 200>><<set $hypnosis_potency++>><<llstress>><<gtiredness>><<gwylanHypnoEffect>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
"On your front," <<he>> says, patting the quilts. "Wings out as far as they'll go without hurting."
<br><br>
You lie down and open them. Gwylan kneels beside your hip, close enough that you feel <<his>> knee against you,
and works the stopper out of the bottle. The smell that comes up is sharp enough to make your eyes water.
<br><br>
<<He>> pours a little into <<his>> palm, rubs both hands together, and lays them flat between your shoulders.
<br><br>
Cold sinks straight through your skin. You suck in a breath, and <<his>> hands follow the muscle outwards,
thumbs turning slow circles at the roots of your wings. The cold turns to heat by the time <<he>> reaches the
first joint. Your wings twitch against the quilts before you can stop them.
<<pain 2>><<arousal 300>><<gpain>><<garousal>>
<br><br>
"Don't hold them stiff," Gwylan says. "Let them be heavy. I'll do the lifting."
<br><br>
<<He>> works out to the next joint, then the next, spreading the oil into every fold and along the ridge of bone.
Whenever you flinch away <<he>> waits, keeping <<his>> hands where they are until you settle, and then carries on.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Gwylan Strong Wings Treatment 3]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Treatment 3
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
<<gwylanHypnoCanvas>>
The heat keeps climbing. Gwylan moves round to kneel at your head, takes both wings by their roots,
and leans <<his>> weight into them.
<br><br>
"Look at my hand. Not at the garden, not at what your back is doing. My hand."
<br><br>
You watch <<his>> fingers open and close, once for each breath you take. <<He>> counts them out loud.
Somewhere after ten you stop keeping track of the numbers. <<hallucinogen 100>><<ghallucinogens>>
<br><br>
<<hypnosisText "The vines and the stone lose their edges. <<His>> hands stay where they are, warm and heavy, while the rest of the garden blurs into colour.">>
<br><br>
"Good. Now listen, because this part is yours." <<His>> voice comes from very close.
"There's muscle in your wings that has never once been asked to work. I'm asking it now, and it's going to fight me."
<br><br>
Something pulls tight under <<his>> thumbs, and it keeps pulling. Deep under the skin the muscle draws in on
itself and sets hard where the oil has soaked in. Your whole back cramps, and your feet push against the quilts. <<pain 3>><<gpain>>
<br><br>
Gwylan keeps talking through it, low and steady, telling you what your body is doing as it happens.
<br><br>
<<link [[Follow <<his>> voice|Gwylan Strong Wings Treatment 4]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings Treatment 4
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
<<gwylanHypnoCanvas>>
"Now the other half," Gwylan says. "The half I can't brew. Go back to the tower for me."
<br><br>
<<hypnosisText "You're on the ledge again, with the wind coming up the wall. The push lands between your shoulders, and then the ground is rushing at you.">>
<br><br>
You know how this part goes: the fall, the noise in your ears, the dark closing in at the edges of your sight.
This time <<his>> hands are on your wings the whole way down, holding them open at the joint where the muscle burns.
<br><br>

"There. That's the moment. The air took your weight and you let it." <<His>> grip tightens.
"Your wings are going to remember doing that. Open them."
<br><br>
Your wings open to their full reach in one stroke. The quilts drag under them, and the beat that
follows lifts your chest clear of the ground before you come back down. Strength runs through muscle that
never had any, and for a second you could swear you feel the wind off the moor under you.
<<willpower 2>><<gwillpower>>
<br><br>
Gwylan strokes the last of the oil into the joints while you lie there breathing into the quilt.
"Hold on to that feeling. Next time the wind gets under you, push down against it. Don't wait to see what
it does with you first."
<br><br>
<<link [[Wake|Gwylan Strong Wings End]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings End
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>><<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "forest_shop">>
<<canvas-model-override "clear">>
You come back a piece at a time. Gwylan is on the quilts beside you, wiping <<his>> hands on a cloth,
and the rest of the garden comes back into focus behind <<him>>.
<br><br>
<<He>> gets an arm around your waist and sits you up. Your wings feel wrong at first, too heavy at the root,
dragging on your shoulders. Then you stretch them, and the rush of air knocks leaves off the vines on the far wall.
<br><br>
Gwylan sits back on <<his>> heels and laughs at the mess. "There. Enough muscle to get you up,
and you already know what to do once you're there."
<br><br>
<<He>> hands you the water jug and waits until you've drunk from it. "Now the part you won't like.
<span class="gold">One week.</span> After that your body wins, the way it always does, and they go back to the
shape it thinks they should be."
<br><br>
You fold the wings in against your back. A week is four trips out to the moor, if the weather holds.
"Can you have a second bottle ready before this one wears off?"
<br><br>
"You can ask, but the answer won't change. New material, three days of preparation, and another afternoon like this one."
<<He>> gathers the bottle and the bowl. "And I can't make it early and leave it on a shelf. It starts dying the moment
I strain it. Neither of us gets to skip a step." <<He>> stands, holding the bowl against <<his>> hip.
"One more thing. My work only holds while the wings do. Lose them and you lose the use of it, and the week
keeps running whether you have them or not."
<br><br>
<<set $gwylan.wingStrength to new DateTime(Time.date).addDays(7).timeStamp>>
<<run delete $gwylan.wingPotionReady>>
<<set $daily.gwylan.hypnosis to true>>
<<set $gwylanSeen.pushUnique("strong_wings_treatment")>>
<<set $_devotionUp to 10 + ($hypnosis_potency || 1)>>
<<gwylanHypnosis "devotion" $_devotionUp>>
<<unset $hypnosis_potency>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Gwylan Strong Wings End 2]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Gwylan Strong Wings End 2
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
<<He>> walks you back through to the shop, keeping a hand at your elbow until you stop wobbling.
<br><br>
<<storeonhandheld "gwylanStrongWings">>
<<gwylanOptions>>

:: Moor Hawk Call
<<effects>>
You climb onto a high rock, cup your hands around your mouth, and make the thin, falling cry Gwylan taught you.
The wind carries it over the heather. You make it again, and wait.
<br><br>
<<moor_hunt_start>>
/* The bird is already on its way, so it arrives after a few moves instead of needing more random sightings. */
<<set $moor_hunt to Math.max($moor_hunt, 7)>>

:: Gwylan Hawk Call
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<run statusCheck("Gwylan")>>
<<npc Gwylan>><<person1>>
You ask how you're meant to find the bird on the moor when it doesn't want to be found.
<br><br>
Gwylan sighs, then cups <<his>> hands around <<his>> mouth and makes a thin, falling cry, like a small
animal that's been hurt. It's a horrible noise. "That's what it listens for. Something weak, out in the open."
<<He>> makes you copy it until the cry falls the way <<hers>> does.
"And don't go dressed like a person with a gun. It hunts, dear. Look like something worth hunting.
Rabbits, for a start. Everything with talons likes a rabbit."
<<set $gwylan.hawkCall to true>>
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You learned a call to draw the great bird's attention. Use it once a day, deeper in the moor.</span>
<<if $preyTrait isnot 0>>
	<br>
	<span class="blue">Visible clothing with the "Prey" trait also makes the bird more likely to find you.</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<gwylanOptions>>
